## Original Content
Tarte Cosmetics is under fire for ways in which it's marketing its new Snatch Stick, with some social-media users accusing the company of "rage baiting" its audience.

## Summary
Tarte Cosmetics is facing backlash for marketing its Snatch Stick product in a way that mirrors plastic surgery. Social media users have accused the company of 'rage baiting' to provoke audience reactions, leading to public criticism.

## Key Points
- Tarte Cosmetics launched the Snatch Stick product with controversial marketing.
- The marketing campaign is accused of mimicking plastic surgery procedures.
- Social media users allege the company is engaging in 'rage baiting' to incite negative attention.
- The incident has sparked public backlash against Tarte Cosmetics.


